    "result_text": "All tests pass and the build succeeds. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI released version 2 of the owner identity, keeping structural impact low \u2014 small edits spread across cohesive units, each in a simple function.\n\n**Identifiers rederived with a `V2` tag (region code mixed in):**\n- `AssignCustomerCode` \u2014 the region embedded in the `memberId` is now `\"V2\" + region` (e.g. `V2NSW261A2B3C4D5`), so no version-1 id is ever reproduced.\n- `HouseholdId` / `IdentityKey` \u2014 a fixed `\"V2|\"` tag is mixed into the hash input, so both change while their call sites and signatures stay untouched (uniqueness comparisons remain consistent since both sides hash the same way).\n\n**User-facing fields stay plain:** In `OwnerMapper`, `locality`, `timezone` and `ownerSegment`'s region now derive from `Locality.of(city, postcode)` (the plain region) instead of extracting the now-V2 region out of the memberId \u2014 so `locality` is still `NSW`, and the `V2` tag never leaks into these.\n\n**Response shape:** `memberId`, `identityKey`, `householdId` are grouped under a new nested `identity` object (new `OwnerIdentity` schema in `openapi.yml`; MapStruct nested-target mappings), removed from the top level, and a top-level integer `apiVersion: 2` was added.\n\n**Audit schema v2:** The structured `OWNER_CREATED` event now carries `\"schemaVersion\":2` and a recomputed `ownerSegment` (from the plain region, per the constraint that `V2` never appears in the segment).\n\n**Files touched (6):** `openapi.yml`, `OwnerMapper.java`, `AssignCustomerCode.java`, `HouseholdId.java`, `IdentityKey.java`, `SaveOwner.java`. Request fields are unchanged.\n\nVerified: `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`. The audit line confirms the new shape:\n`{\"seq\":1,\"schemaVersion\":2,\"ownerId\":11,\"memberId\":\"V2NSW2716E6609E7\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"ownerSegment\":\"STANDARD_METRO\",\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}`",
